+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+Two of the findings below are ship-blockers on their own. `deposit()` **cannot succeed
+against the real USDT contract** — the vault would be deployed as a brick that reverts on
+every single deposit. And the vault **never credits Aave interest to anyone**, so even if
+deposits worked, a depositor who held for a year would get back *less* than they put in.
+
+Everything here is demonstrated against the contract exactly as it stands. Nothing under
+`src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` or `test/mocks/` was modified.
+
+---
+
+## Why the existing 39 tests and 100% coverage don't catch any of this
+
+The coverage number is real. I reproduced it:
+
+```
+$ forge coverage --no-match-path "test/{ForkMainnet,AuditInvariant,AuditAccounting}.t.sol"
+| File                        | % Lines         | % Statements    | % Branches    | % Funcs         |
+| src/UsdtYieldVault.sol      | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57)  | 85.71% (6/7)  | 100.00% (11/11) |
+```
+
+100% of lines and 100% of functions execute. The problem is not which lines run, it's *what
+they run against*. The suite only ever runs against two stand-ins:
+
+- **`test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol`** is a plain OpenZeppelin `ERC20`. It returns `true` from
+  `approve()`. **Real USDT returns nothing at all** — that single difference is F-01, and it
+  is fatal.
+- **`test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol`** mints aTokens 1:1 and never accrues a cent of interest.
+  A vault whose entire purpose is yield is tested against a pool that pays no yield, so
+  F-02 — the fact that yield is silently discarded — is structurally invisible.
+
+Every assertion in the existing suite is of the form "the code did what the code does".
+None of them assert a *property a depositor cares about*: that they get their money back,
+that they earn the yield, that the vault can pay what it says it owes.
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce everything
+
+I added four new files, all under `test/`:
+
+| File | What it is |
+| --- | --- |
+| `test/ForkMainnet.t.sol` | Runs against **real mainnet state** — the real USDT, the real Aave V3 pool, real aToken interest accrual. |
+| `test/AuditMocks.sol` | Local stand-ins. Deliberately identical to the existing mocks except the Aave pool can accrue interest. |
+| `test/AuditAccounting.t.sol` | Unit/fuzz tests for the accounting and access-control findings. |
+| `test/AuditInvariant.t.sol` | Stateful invariant campaign. |
+
+The only thing I changed outside `test/` is `foundry.toml`, to add an RPC endpoint for the
+fork tests:
+
+```toml
+[rpc_endpoints]
+mainnet = "https://eth.drpc.org"
+```
+
+Substitute your own archive RPC if you prefer. The fork tests pin block **25,780,000** so
+the numbers below are deterministic.
+
+> **Two notes on exact-matching my output.** Fuzz tests use a random seed per run, so the
+> `μ`/`~` gas figures on `testFuzz_*` lines will differ slightly from what I pasted; the
+> pass/fail result and all `console.log` values are deterministic. Likewise the shrunk
+> counterexample sequence for `invariant_B` will differ from mine — what reproduces is the
+> failure itself, with a non-zero unreachable balance.
+>
+> **Note on re-running the invariant suite:** Foundry caches invariant failures. Run
+> `rm -rf cache/invariant` before `forge test --match-path test/AuditInvariant.t.sol`,
+> otherwise you will see a "replay failure" instead of a fresh campaign.
